	<key>readme</key>
	<string>## Mole

Runs [Mole](https://mole.fit) (`brew install mole`). Uninstalling and cleaning run in the background: Mole's confirmation is answered for you and the result arrives as a notification.

**`mole`**: Mole commands

| Item | ↩ | ⌥↩ (dry run, in Ghostty) | ⌘↩ |
| Open Mole | `mo` in Ghostty | | |
| Clean | `mo clean` in the background | `mo clean --dry-run` | |
| Uninstall an app… | search apps (`uninstall`) | | `mo uninstall` (Mole's picker, in Ghostty) |
| Last run log | open the output of the last background run | | |

**`uninstall`**: lists every app Mole can uninstall, A–Z, with its size. Type to filter.

| Key | Action |
| ↩ | `mo uninstall &amp;lt;app&amp;gt;` in the background, no confirmation |
| ⌥↩ | Dry run in Ghostty: preview what would be removed |
| ⌘↩ | Reveal in Finder |
| ⌘C | Copy the app's path |

Removed files go to the Trash. If Mole needs admin rights (Homebrew casks, apps owned by root), a password dialog appears; Cancel stops without changing anything. Runs queue up, one at a time.

`mo clean` skips system caches that need admin rights unless *System caches* is enabled in the workflow configuration.

The app list comes from `mo uninstall --list`, which takes about 10 seconds. It is cached and refreshed in the background whenever an app folder changes, and at least every 6 hours.</string>
